LESSON 14: ERRORS

AN ERROR REPORT HAS THREE LINES: THE KIND OF ERROR, THE
STATEMENT, AND A CARET UNDER THE POINT APL HAD REACHED WHEN
IT GAVE UP. APL WORKS FROM THE RIGHT, SO EVERYTHING TO THE
RIGHT OF THE CARET WAS DONE. TRY:

      1 2+1 2 3
      2÷0
      XYZ+1
      (1 2 3)[5]
(TRY IT. TYPE GO TO GO ON, OR STOP TO LEAVE.)
⎕:
      1 2+1 2 3
LENGTH ERROR
      1 2+1 2 3
         ^
⎕:
      2÷0
DOMAIN ERROR
      2÷0
       ^
⎕:
      XYZ+1
VALUE ERROR
      XYZ+1
      ^
⎕:
      GO
THE COMMON KINDS:

   SYNTAX     THE LINE IS NOT A SENTENCE: 2+ OR ((1)
   VALUE      A NAME WITH NO VALUE, OR A FUNCTION WITH NONE
   DOMAIN     THE RIGHT SHAPE, THE WRONG KIND: 2÷0, 'A'+1
   LENGTH     TWO VECTORS OF DIFFERENT LENGTHS
   RANK       A VECTOR AGAINST A MATRIX: 1 2 3+2 2⍴1
   INDEX      A SUBSCRIPT PAST THE END

AT A PAUSE, OR AT THE PROMPT, AN ERROR IS REPORTED AND YOU
GO ON. INSIDE A FUNCTION IT IS DIFFERENT.
(TRY IT. TYPE GO TO GO ON, OR STOP TO LEAVE.)
⎕:
      GO
OOPS FAILS ON ITS SECOND LINE:

      ∇OOPS
[1]   'BEFORE'
[2]   1 2+1 2 3
[3]   'AFTER'
[4]   ∇

